<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Telmex cut by Paribas.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Telmex cut by Paribas.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Paribas Capital Markets said on Friday it had downgraded Telfonos de Mexico to overvalued-sell from fairly valued-no action, its designation for hold.</p>
<p>-- Analyst William Beavington told Reuters, &quot;This stock offers no visible growth in U.S.-dollar earnings until 1999.&quot;</p>
<p>-- He said Telmex's stock had underperformed the Mexican market in dollar terms since December 1995. &quot;I see nothing on the 12-month horizon which is going to change that,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Ian Simpson, Wall Street Desk (212) 859-1730</p>
</text>
